# Commission-input delivery: implementation acceptance

2026-10-27, root coordinator. This account concerns C's original-undertaking
feature. The subsequent self-audit and later result inspection are separate.

The Rust crate implements `accept`, `complete`, `inspect`, `read` and `abandon`.
Its guide gives the exact finite-file request, supported roles, explicit grants
and limits, receipt reference, custody boundary and failure behavior. The named
manager preserves the delivered bundle. No audit launch, result custody, future
result format, automatic disposal or general retained store was implemented.
The Python runtime and bundled resources remain unchanged.

Release binary SHA-256:
`b057d64cf010c28554ae087b2da4f4ae5ac8b0834ea8bed863d3cfcc99ddd1b2`.
Observed host: Apple Silicon macOS 26.7.1, Rust/Cargo 1.99.0. Runtime dependencies
are compiled into the executable; the pinned build dependencies were available
offline. The implementation worker returned and stopped; root reviewed the
core acceptance, readback and disposition paths and independently tested a copy
of the release executable.

## Evidence and disposition

- Worker integration: **14/14 tests passed**, retained in
  `successor/evidence/test-03.*`, with fixtures/streams in that directory.
  `IMPLEMENTATION-02.json` binds source and release identities. Earlier compiler
  failures and 10/12-test checkpoints remain unchanged.
- Independent installed executable: **46/46 checks passed** in
  `.scratch/commission-intake-01/acceptance-02/RESULT.json`, with command streams,
  copied binary, input witnesses and the unrelated working-directory locator.
  Checks include command outcomes as well as behavioral predicates; this is not
  46 independent experimental cases or a whole-product correctness claim.
- The independent cases recover exact question/material/guidance/request bytes,
  survive original source-path loss and bundle relocation, distinguish a changed
  selected operand with other request coordinates fixed, and keep the receipt
  invariant when only the destination changes. Two real SIGKILL invocations
  fired after a large payload was observed: explicit completion preserves prior
  partial files, and attributed incomplete disposition preserves them without
  later acceptance. The independent witness stays outside the changed specimens.
- Selected damage, external receipt mismatch, duplicate escaped JSON keys,
  symlink ancestors, special files, changed intent and completed lost-reply lookup
  were exercised. A verified question remained recoverable when a different
  payload was corrupted; the qualification disclosed whole-bundle damage.

Root's earlier independent run passed 44/44 on the preceding binary. Source
review then found ordinary acceptance could resume after intent but before the
first attempt, and disposition validation differed between observation and
mutations. Both were corrected with focused tests: only explicit `complete`
continues a prior incomplete intent, and shared validation preserves malformed,
unsupported and misbound disposition diagnostics. The final independent run used
the revised binary and a stronger operand/destination comparison. Earlier results
and specimens remain evidence of their actual coverage, not of the final build.

The frozen Python writer was separately checked with the required installed-wheel
runner: **63 selected / 63 passed** across handoff, triage and input tests, at
`.scratch/commission-intake-01/frozen-custody-check-01.json`. This qualifies the
chosen existing custody route's tested behaviors, not C. The exact tested wheel
was installed for the study. An initial launch tried its default manager home
outside the permitted workspace and was refused; that diagnostic remains.
Startup with an explicit fresh permitted manager home succeeded. The environment
and wheel identity are in `AUDIT-ENVIRONMENT.json` beside those records.

## Limits and next work

The implementation uses descriptor-relative no-follow reads, exclusive receipts,
syncs and cooperative advisory mutation locks. These are not evidence of
host-wide confinement, malicious-host safety, replication, historical actor
authentication or power-loss durability. Linux and WSL have not been qualified.
Readback never executes the old writer; incomplete mutation remains bound to
the recorded binary. Acknowledging a corrupted original intent remains unresolved
and does not silently discharge the original undertaking.

This supports using C for the actual self-audit commission. It does not certify
the intellectual utility of the audit or require its later return to be fully
inspectable. Root owns the named retained evidence and original witnesses through
review. No pruning or production custody close has occurred. Next: freeze the
actual audit subject, commission it through the existing Python workflow, recover
its commission in a fresh manager context, preserve its actual return through
that existing process, and observe a fresh investigator's needs and limitations.
